--TEST--
`Core\Csv::rows` over a walk of chunks gives the records before a field that is not UTF-8 in the second chunk, then throws a `ParseError` that names its line — `rule:types/string-is-utf8`, `rule:core-api/a-member-takes-the-source-the-program-holds`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Csv::rows
// The second chunk is "um", a new line, "bad", the byte FF and a new line.
// The byte FF never appears in UTF-8.
array<bytes> $chunks = [
    "name\nfig\npl" as bytes,
    Core\Bytes::pack('CCCCCCCC', 0x75, 0x6D, 0x0A, 0x62, 0x61, 0x64, 0xFF, 0x0A),
    "last\n" as bytes,
];
int $given = 0;
try {
    foreach (Core\Csv::rows($chunks) as array<string> $record) {
        $given = $given + 1;
        echo "got ", $record["0"], "\n";
    }
    echo "the byte FF was read as text\n";
} catch (ParseError $notText) {
    echo $notText->message, "\n";
}
echo "given before the error: ", $given, "\n";
--EXPECT--
got name
got fig
got plum
Core\Csv::rows: line 4 of the source has a field that is not valid UTF-8
given before the error: 3
